HOW TO IDENTIFY WHICH TYPE — DECISION GUIDE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Read the problem. Ask these questions in order:

Does the problem involve prerequisites / task ordering?
→ YES → Type 3 (Topological Sort)

Does it ask for minimum cost or minimum steps?
→ Equal edge weights (or unweighted) → Type 2A (BFS)
→ Different edge weights → Type 2B (Dijkstra)

Does it involve dynamically merging groups, or cycle in undirected?
→ YES → Type 4 (Union-Find)

Does it ask to split nodes into 2 conflicting groups?
Or detect a cycle in a directed graph?
→ YES → Type 5 (Bipartite / DFS 3-state)

None of the above (connectivity, island count, reachability)?
→ Type 1 (BFS / DFS)

